    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d301">

                <pb facs="1358" n="1253" xml:id="pg1253"/>

                <head>301. Memorandum From Washburn (USIA) to Cutler<anchor n="1" xml:id="d301-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1958-03-25">March 25, 1958</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d301-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d301-1"/>
                <p>USIA feels very strongly that unless the
                    President can state that the open shot at Eniwetok will be 90% fallout-free or
                    better—and unless AEC is sure it will be at
                    least that clean—it would be better for the United States <hi
                        rendition="#italic">not</hi> to hold the shot.</p>
                <p>The President has already publicly used the figure of 96%.</p>
                <p>If the 6 megaton shot is 95% clean, it will still yield 300,000 tons of fission
                    contamination—or the equivalent of 15 Hiroshima bombs.</p>
                <p>If it is 90% clean, it will still yield as much fallout contamination as 30
                    Hiroshimas.</p>
                <p>Any “cleanliness” less than this, in our judgment, would be far more embarrassing
                    to the President and to the United States than having to find some reason for
                    not holding an open shot at this time.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Abbott
                            Washburn</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Acting Director</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">United States Information Agency</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
